Z||000024||houlster||08-06-99||06:45 PM||||Acording to "Chevy Power"...<p>"The only difference between the standard and H.O. cast iron heads is the size of the valves; the ports and combustion chambers are the same in both cylinder heads."<p>So, if the ports are the same size there should be no problem cutting the valve holes bigger right?<br>
